<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Continuation War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a>–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Continuation War was the conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> from June 1941 to September 1944, fought alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s invasion of the Soviet Union. Finland recovered the lands lost in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/winter-war">Winter War</a> and occupied much of Soviet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a>, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrozavodsk">Petrozavodsk</a>. After a Soviet offensive in 1944 it signed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> Armistice, ceding Karelia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petsamo">Petsamo</a> but remaining independent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/continuation-war.jpg" alt="Continuation War" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sot.virk. Uuno Laukka · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finnish_soldiers_1944.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
